<title>USA: WestPoint Stevens to pay $360,000 over Pima charge.</title>
<headline>WestPoint Stevens to pay $360,000 over Pima charge.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>WestPoint-Stevens Inc has agreed to pay a $360,000 civil penalty to settle Federal Trade Commission charges that it violated the Textile Fiber Products Identification Act, the FTC said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The penalty, a record in such a case, settles charges the company misrepresented the amount of premium Pima cotton its sheets and towels contained, the FTC said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said that items sold as being pure Pima had ranged in Pima content from six to 50 percent.</p>
</text>
